# Memory Tab Unlock Rule (Absolute)

The **Memory** tab must **never** appear before the World Choir live event is finished.

## When Memory may unlock

- Only after the active event song has ended (`EventState.COMPLETED` / post-event).
- Users can then open Memory and the post-event experience.

## When Memory must stay hidden

- Before the event (countdown / waiting)
- During final hour / warm-up
- During the live event itself (pre-event video + song)

## Implementation constraints

- Do **not** set `MEMORY_PREVIEW_MODE = true` unless the user explicitly asks to design Memory while the event is still upcoming, and turn it back off afterward.
- Do **not** bypass `WorldChoirConfig.isMemoryUnlocked()` or `WorldChoirNav.guardMemoryRoute()`.
- Do **not** show Memory in nav, deep-link into `memory.html`, or treat Memory as available pre-event.
- When changing test event times, keep Memory gated by real event completion — never unlock Memory early as a side effect.

## Temporary test schedule note

While `TEMP_EVENT_TEST_OVERRIDE_ENABLED` is true, event start is a same-day UTC test time (not official 2027-09-21). Memory still unlocks only **after that test event ends**. Official date returns to **21 September 2027** when the user asks to restore it.
